===== PHASE 3 DECISION =====
base_impostor (Devilx86/ImpostorModmenu) - CLONED, REJECTED AS NATIVE BASE:
 - last commit 2021-06-25; targets Among Us ~v2020.11-2021.4
 - hook addresses are hardcoded uintptr_t literals in app/src/main/cpp/func.h (only two arch tables:
   armeabi-v7a and arm64-v8a), no runtime signature resolution -> invalid for 2026.11.3
 - illegal write path: func.h resolves rpcSetScanner / rpcRepairSystem / repairSystem /
   rpcMurderPlayer via getAbsoluteAddress(...,true) i.e. write-to-.text at those literals.
   On 2026.11.3 those literals point into unrelated code/data => SIGSEGV at startup.
 - 5 of its 10 patch/critical targets no longer exist (see offsets.json legacy_absent_in_this_build)
 - outputs .so is gitignored/absent; would require NDK+gradle to build, then still fail on offsets
 => cannot "compile cleanly against the current game version". Rejected on evidence, not guesswork.
base_malum (AstralKitsune/MalumMenu-Android) - CLONED, ACCEPTED AS THE BASE:
 - pushed 2026-11-07 (current); version targeted 2.1.1
 - TS/Frida on frida-il2cpp-bridge + frida-java-menu: resolves classes/methods BY NAME at runtime,
   so it survives the renames found in phase 2 (Kill->MurderPlayer etc.) without offset patching
 - README explicitly states its default build CANNOT coexist with the official app
   ("Do I need to uninstall the original Among Us? A: Currently yes, as it has the same package name")
   -> our job is exactly the piece it lacks: full package rename + core-library injection.

