===== PHASE 7: MENU-VISIBILITY FIX (agent 1.0.1) =====
Symptom reported on device: stock-looking Among Us (US build), no menu at all;
overlay/"Display over other apps" permission was surfaced by the previous build.

ROOT CAUSES (found in the bundled library + our entrypoint, both verified in source):
 1) frida-java-menu/dist/menu.js : Composer constructor
      if (!overlay.check()) { overlay.ask(); setTimeout(async () => (await activityInstance).finish(), 3000); }
    SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW is never pre-granted on a fresh install -> the constructor
    opened the settings screen and then finished the activity after 3 s, and
    WindowManager.addView(TYPE_APPLICATION_OVERLAY) was rejected (BadTokenException,
    swallowed by show()'s catch) -> no menu, ever, without a manual appops grant.
 2) index.ts built MenuUI.init() ONLY inside Il2Cpp.perform(); any module init
    throw (or a failed IL2CPP bootstrap) meant the UI was never constructed.
 3) Game.cls() cached null class lookups made before assemblies were resolved
    (build order above), so even a late-initialised il2cpp would stay unusable.
 4) LayoutConfig.ts called systemAccentColor() at script-load time (Java/context
    access during module evaluation) - removed, static colour used.

FIX:
 - MenuUI rewritten as an IN-WINDOW panel: added to the activity's
   android.R.id.content FrameLayout as a sibling above Unity's SurfaceView.
   No overlay permission, no WindowManager, no Composer instance.
   Layout: titled panel + ScrollView with all 11 previous sections + DIAGNOSTICS.
   "✕" hides the panel and shows an in-window "MOD" button; "–" collapses the body.
   Panel is clickable (blocks game input under it only); all other screen areas
   still pass touches to Unity. 4 s watchdog re-attaches if content view changes.
 - index.ts: UI first (pure Java), IL2CPP modules after, each in try/catch;
   MenuUI.refreshHost() re-enables host-only widgets once IL2CPP is ready.
 - Bridge.ts added: activity discovery by polling Java.choose (no Activity hooks),
   content-view lookup, dp/screen helpers, main-thread marshalling.
 - Logger.ts: persists every line to
   /sdcard/Android/data/com.innersloth.spacemafia.mod/files/modmenu.log
   and exposes tail()/path()/clear() for the in-menu DIAGNOSTICS section.
 - Game.cls(): no caching while an assembly image is still unresolved.

